Subject: utility-private.h: popen_utf8() returns NULL on wasi

wasi-libc has no popen().  popen_utf8() is a `static inline` in a header that
every coder pulls in, so even though MAGICKCORE_HAVE_POPEN is undefined and no
caller is compiled, the body still has to typecheck -- and it doesn't (implicit
`int popen()` returned as `FILE *`).

Returning NULL is the graceful failure the callers already handle: blob.c turns
it into "UnableToOpenBlob" and delegate.c falls back to system(), which patch
0004 stubs out to -1.

--- a/MagickCore/utility-private.h
+++ b/MagickCore/utility-private.h
@@ -154,8 +154,13 @@
 static inline FILE *popen_utf8(const char *command,const char *type)
 {
-#if !defined(MAGICKCORE_WINDOWS_SUPPORT) || defined(__CYGWIN__)
+#if defined(__wasi__)
+  /* No processes under WASI: fail the way a refused pipe would. */
+  (void) command;
+  (void) type;
+  return((FILE *) NULL);
+#elif !defined(MAGICKCORE_WINDOWS_SUPPORT) || defined(__CYGWIN__)
   return(popen(command,type));
 #else
   return(NTOpenPipeWide(command,type));
 #endif
 }
